Chapter: Cce Builtin Bounds

 The probe codes are the three that separate the bands, plus a digit: 12
 (a digit), 15 (the letter a), 70 (punctuation, the hole between the
 bands), 97 (accented e, the widened band). The 70 cell is the control
 that matters: a rebuilt builtin that swallowed the punctuation hole
 answers T there.

 is-whitespace is here for the same reason and is the same kind of claim:
 the band is 1..2 and NUL sits below it, so the 0 cell is what separates a
 corrected builtin from the `<= 2` one it replaced.

Section: Cells

  cbb-letter : Integer -> Text
  cbb-letter (n) = if is-letter (code-to-char n) then "T" else "F"

  cbb-ws : Integer -> Text
  cbb-ws (n) = if is-whitespace (code-to-char n) then "T" else "F"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni ("builtin-letter 12,15,70,97: " & cbb-letter 12 & cbb-letter 15 & cbb-letter 70 & cbb-letter 97)
   print-line-uni ("builtin-ws 0,1,2,3: " & cbb-ws 0 & cbb-ws 1 & cbb-ws 2 & cbb-ws 3)
  end

